<http://data.silknow.org/object/590f5481-9e0c-330a-9556-1a95b06b0c7e/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Bath wrap of embroidered linen with silk in double running in steps and double running variations (outlines and stems) and with metal thread in double darning on the diagonal. Made from three widths. Each width is decorated with four bands of embroidered motifs. There are two motifs which alternate within the bands horizontally and vertically: The first is a  flower with a gold centre and eight pink petals which seem to rotate around the centre, and the second has seven light pink star-like flowers which surround a closed bud in pink and light blue. There are smaller floral motifs scattered on the ground. It seems that the motifs were individually block-printed onto the ground because the alignment varies."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/590f5481-9e0c-330a-9556-1a95b06b0c7e> .

